## Predictions (written before the run)
- a mid-predator class is buildable: badgers are present in both arms; the armed badger kills small prey and vermin (groundhog, skunk, porcupine, rats) and never a citizen, a fort animal, or anything above its own weight
- the flag makes a general predator: badgers present in both arms; the armed badger attacks whatever it meets, including large animals and the fort's own, so the class needs a SIZE FILTER on the relation targets rather than just the caste flag
- the flag moves the species into DF's large-predator pool: badgers arrive in the CONTROL arm but not in the armed one — the wiki's rule is that a biome supports about seven large-predator species chosen by a d100 under FREQUENCY, and a badger at frequency 5 would rarely win a slot, so arming a mid-predator would make it RARER rather than fiercer and the class cannot be built on the flag at all
- the badger is armed but never meets anything: badgers present, zero attacks in both arms; the coupling needs prey written within the nudge radius rather than left to chance

